    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-efficiency pairing of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Kyle Tucker** (74.44). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from an optimal #2 spot and a favorable dynamic platoon advantage against Holmes, while **Kyle Tucker** is primed to exploit a weak 5.63 xERA matchup against Gasser, offsetting the risk of a neutral platoon. **Andy Pages** (69.18) and **Josh Jung** (64.46) also represent high-floor assets; **Josh Jung**, assuming he holds the #2 spot in a projected favorable matchup against Ure\u00f1a, offers excellent value despite the lingering \"Lineup Pending\" status. These four hitters form our primary engine, leveraging distinct SP skill edges to maintain efficiency across the board.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Nolan Schanuel** (44.78), who ultimately failed to crack the starting nine due to the oppressive presence of Nathan Eovaldi (3.19 xERA). While **Nolan Schanuel** remains a viable depth piece, the optimizer favored the higher volatility/upside of **Nasim Nunez** (58.15) and **Dominic Smith** (59.08) against mid-tier pitching. We are exercising caution with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.94), whose base projection is cannibalized by an elite encounter with Skenes; he occupies the UTIL slot largely for his raw talent, but the matchup against a sub-3.00 xERA arm significantly lowers his floor. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson**, all of whom remain sidelined on the IL, leaving our current active rotation to shoulder the burden of our 5x5 Roto standing.",
